  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>The GitHub actions workflow “Build Main Branch” seems to build Docker images in the deploy job, but never pushes them to Docker Hub.</p>\n\n<p>The last execution of the workflow from <tt>2026-04-08</tt> (<a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/actions/runs/24147566494/job/70470612272\" title=\"smart-link\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://github.com/fcrepo/fcrepo/actions/runs/24147566494/job/70470612272</a>) shows the following warning in the step “Deploy Docker Image”:</p>\n\n<div class=\"preformatted panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"preformattedContent panelContent\">\n<pre>WARNING: No output specified with docker-container driver. Build result will only remain in the build cache. To push result image into registry use --push or to load image into docker use --load</pre>\n</div></div>\n\n\n\n<p>Analysis: The script <a href=\"https://github.com/fcrepo-exts/fcrepo-docker/blob/main/build-and-push-to-dockerhub.sh\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">build-and-push-to-dockerhub.sh from fcrepo-exts/fcrepo-docker</a> used to build the Docker image, only pushes the Image to Docker Hub, when the command line flag <tt>--push</tt> as been specified. This flag is currently missing in the workflow.</p>",
